cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite it as below, and cite Calhoun (1973) for the experiment
  it simulates.
title: "Universe 25 simulation: an agent-based model of Calhoun's mouse colony"
type: software
authors:
  - alias: ji-hun-git
repository-code: "https://github.com/ji-hun-git/universe-25-simulation"
url: "https://github.com/ji-hun-git/universe-25-simulation"
license: MIT
version: 0.2.0
date-released: "2026-11-25"
abstract: >-
  An agent-based simulation of Universe 25, John B. Calhoun's 1968-1973 mouse colony with
  unlimited resources. Each mouse eats, drinks, nests, courts, fights, nurses and grows stressed
  in a model of Calhoun's pen. The colony is fitted to the published record: on 48 unseen seeds,
  11 of 14 population and timeline numbers fall inside the model's 5-95 % range, and 46 of 48
  runs rise and collapse. The behavioural categories Calhoun reported are not reproduced.
keywords:
  - Universe 25
  - mouse utopia
  - behavioral sink
  - John B. Calhoun
  - agent-based model
  - population dynamics
  - population collapse
  - animal behavior
references:
  - type: article
    authors:
      - family-names: Calhoun
        given-names: John B.
    title: "Death squared: the explosive growth and demise of a mouse population"
    journal: "Proceedings of the Royal Society of Medicine"
    volume: 66
    issue: "1 Pt 2"
    start: 80
    end: 88
    year: 1973
